<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Privacy Policy - Quick Broadcast</title>
</head>
<body>

<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p>Effective date: 18 August 2026</p>

<p>
Quick Broadcast is developed by <strong>X127</strong>. We respect your privacy
and are committed to handling personal information responsibly. This policy
explains what information Quick Broadcast uses, why it is used, and the choices
available to you.
</p>

<h2>1. What Quick Broadcast Does</h2>

<p>
Quick Broadcast helps parents, guardians, and family members send household
messages and receive delivery and acknowledgement updates. Family groups are
private and are not visible to the public.
</p>

<h2>2. Information We Collect and Use</h2>

<p>Quick Broadcast may collect and store the following information to provide its service:</p>

<ul>
    <li>Display names and family-group membership</li>
    <li>Parent recovery email addresses, where provided</li>
    <li>Account and device identifiers needed for sign-in, pairing, and notifications</li>
    <li>Notification tokens used to deliver broadcasts to paired devices</li>
    <li>Broadcast messages, recipients, delivery status, and acknowledgements</li>
    <li>Quick-broadcast choices, widget shortcuts, preferences, and colour-theme settings</li>
</ul>

<p>
This information is used only to operate Quick Broadcast, including pairing
devices, delivering messages, showing acknowledgement status, restoring family
access, and improving reliability.
</p>

<h2>3. Children and Family Use</h2>

<p>
Quick Broadcast is designed for parents and guardians to coordinate with their
household. It may be used by children, including children under 13, as part of
a family group set up and managed by a parent or guardian.
</p>

<p>
Children do not create public profiles or communicate with strangers through
Quick Broadcast. A parent or guardian controls family membership and which
devices are paired to a child profile.
</p>

<p>
Quick Broadcast does not sell personal information, use targeted advertising,
or knowingly use children’s information for advertising purposes.
</p>

<h2>4. Third-Party Services</h2>

<p>
Quick Broadcast uses trusted services provided by Google Firebase, including
Firebase Authentication, Cloud Firestore, Cloud Functions, and Firebase Cloud
Messaging. On Apple devices, notifications may also be delivered through Apple
Push Notification service.
</p>

<p>
These providers process information as necessary to provide their services and
in accordance with their own privacy policies.
</p>

<h2>5. Purchases</h2>

<p>
If Premium subscriptions or purchases are offered, payments are processed by
the Apple App Store or Google Play Store. Quick Broadcast does not collect or
store your payment-card details.
</p>

<h2>6. Data Sharing</h2>

<p>
Information is shared only with members of your private family group where
needed for the app to work, such as showing a broadcast message or its delivery
and acknowledgement status. We do not sell personal information or share it
with advertisers.
</p>

<h2>7. Data Security</h2>

<p>
We use reasonable technical measures and trusted cloud-service providers to
protect information. However, no internet-based service can guarantee complete
security.
</p>

<h2>8. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>

<p>
You can delete your Quick Broadcast account and associated data from the app’s
Account Settings. Deleting a family-owner account removes the associated family
data. You may also contact us for help with a deletion request.
</p>

<h2>9. Changes to This Policy</h2>

<p>
We may update this policy when Quick Broadcast changes or legal requirements
change. The latest version will always be published at this page.
</p>

<h2>10. Contact Us</h2>

<p>
For privacy questions or deletion assistance, contact:
</p>

<p><strong>x127.scott@gmail.com</strong></p>

</body>
</html>
